<title>URUGUAY: Uruguayan consumer prices up 2.0 pct in January.</title>
<headline>Uruguayan consumer prices up 2.0 pct in January.</headline>
<dateline>MONTEVIDEO 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Uruguay's consumer prices rose 2.0 percent in January, bringing the annual inflation rate in the last 12 months to 24.3 percent, the National Statistics Institute said Wednesday.</p>
<p>The figure compared with a monthly rise of 2.0 percent in January 1996 and an increase of 1.2 percent in December.</p>
<p>Uruguay's inflation rate was 24.3 in 1996. The government has an inflation target of 17 percent for 1997.</p>
<p>--Montevideo Newsroom + 5982 92 03 36</p>
